I'm assuming this is the same
for you, you get on the bus,

00:56:00.980 --> 00:56:03.260
we get to wait 30 minutes
for it to fucking go.

00:56:03.260 --> 00:56:06.400
And then, 'cause it was peak
traffic hours at this point,

00:56:06.400 --> 00:56:10.000
it took an hour and a half
to get to the fucking hotel.

00:56:10.000 --> 00:56:10.833
So not fun.

00:56:10.833 --> 00:56:12.660
But where was your hotel?

00:56:12.660 --> 00:56:14.100
- I can't remember where my hotel was,

00:56:14.100 --> 00:56:15.076
but it was a different one.

00:56:15.076 --> 00:56:16.937
- They blindfolded me in the bus.

00:56:16.937 --> 00:56:18.650
- Honestly, I got in the bus

00:56:18.650 --> 00:56:20.403
and I just like fucking conked out.

00:56:20.403 --> 00:56:22.097
- Oh really?
- Yeah, yeah.

00:56:22.097 --> 00:56:22.930
It was like Squid Game 'cause I was like.

00:56:22.930 --> 00:56:26.150
- 'Cause it had the squid game music.

00:56:26.150 --> 00:56:27.530
- They didn't need to gas me.

00:56:27.530 --> 00:56:28.917
I fucking conked out myself.

00:56:28.917 --> 00:56:31.326
Like, Jesus, fuck.
- Woke up on a bunk bed.

00:56:31.326 --> 00:56:32.900
(all laughing)

00:56:32.900 --> 00:56:35.300
- If they could have
gassed us, they would have.

00:56:37.686 --> 00:56:40.260
- Congratulations, you're
here on quarantine day one.

00:56:40.260 --> 00:56:41.230
- They took us-

00:56:41.230 --> 00:56:42.643
- Only half of you will survive.

00:56:42.643 --> 00:56:45.230
(all laughing)

00:56:45.230 --> 00:56:48.650
- They took us all the
way from Haneda Airport,

00:56:48.650 --> 00:56:51.190
which is like very south
of Tokyo to Ryogoku.

00:56:52.573 --> 00:56:54.120
- Ryogoku?
- Ryogoku.

00:56:54.120 --> 00:56:55.730
- That's like an hour and a half away.

00:56:55.730 --> 00:56:57.910
- It was like North Tokyo.
- Yeah.

00:56:57.910 --> 00:57:00.090
- And I've never been to Ryogoku before.

00:57:00.090 --> 00:57:00.923
And it was literally,

00:57:00.923 --> 00:57:02.610
we were staying right on
top of the Sumo stadium.

00:57:02.610 --> 00:57:03.690
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:57:03.690 --> 00:57:05.670
- Okay, mine was like 20
minutes away from the airport.

00:57:05.670 --> 00:57:06.503
- Motherfucker!

00:57:08.054 --> 00:57:08.887
And so, yeah.

00:57:08.887 --> 00:57:11.200
We'll get into how good
your treatment was, Garnt.

00:57:12.120 --> 00:57:15.750
So, we get to this hotel
and I shit you not,

00:57:15.750 --> 00:57:19.060
there is like 40 armed
guards at this hotel,

00:57:19.060 --> 00:57:20.220
for like 20 of us.

00:57:20.220 --> 00:57:21.779
It was ridiculous.

00:57:21.779 --> 00:57:22.612
- It's like literally Squid Game.

00:57:22.612 --> 00:57:25.420
- It was literally like 40 armed guards.

00:57:25.420 --> 00:57:29.610
And all they did is you
watch you get off this bus.

00:57:29.610 --> 00:57:32.280
And they're watching you the whole time.

00:57:32.280 --> 00:57:34.260
But again, presumably I don't know why,

00:57:34.260 --> 00:57:36.402
like this seems excessive.

00:57:36.402 --> 00:57:37.800
- I don't even think the prison system

00:57:37.800 --> 00:57:40.020
has that many fucking guards.

00:57:40.020 --> 00:57:41.830
- These hotels have been
completely converted

00:57:41.830 --> 00:57:44.020
into COVID hotels.

00:57:44.020 --> 00:57:45.920
They're closed to the public.

00:57:45.920 --> 00:57:47.560
There's one right in Shinjuku Sanchome,

00:57:47.560 --> 00:57:50.480
I walked past it, and I saw all the guards

00:57:50.480 --> 00:57:52.130
and with all their face masks on.

00:57:53.600 --> 00:57:54.620
And it was just weird.

00:57:54.620 --> 00:57:56.300
You have to wait, again.

00:57:56.300 --> 00:57:57.490
You have to wait for fuck's sake,

00:57:57.490 --> 00:57:58.940
you have to wait another 30 minutes.

00:57:58.940 --> 00:58:02.150
Finally you get to a table
where a woman talks to you.

00:58:02.150 --> 00:58:05.030
And she was explaining what
you could and couldn't do,

00:58:05.030 --> 00:58:06.540
but her English was really bad,

00:58:06.540 --> 00:58:07.520
and obviously again,

00:58:07.520 --> 00:58:10.170
I know this is my fault,
I don't speak Japanese,

00:58:10.170 --> 00:58:12.880
but I asked her a question

00:58:12.880 --> 00:58:15.618
and then she just got really like, "What?"

00:58:15.618 --> 00:58:16.451
She like didn't understand that.

00:58:16.451 --> 00:58:19.350
And I was like, "Oh, maybe
I can ask someone else?"

00:58:19.350 --> 00:58:21.223
And I felt really bad, but
then someone else came over

00:58:21.223 --> 00:58:22.730
and who spoke perfect English.

00:58:22.730 --> 00:58:23.563
And I was like,

00:58:23.563 --> 00:58:24.640
"So come on, tell me what's going on?

00:58:24.640 --> 00:58:25.580
What am I doing here, man?"

00:58:25.580 --> 00:58:28.450
And also, this whole time,
during this whole thing,

00:58:28.450 --> 00:58:31.077
I kept asking everyone at
every single checkpoint,

00:58:31.077 --> 00:58:33.880
"Do you know how many days
I'm spending in this hotel?"

00:58:33.880 --> 00:58:35.490
'Cause they said three days, right?

00:58:35.490 --> 00:58:37.060
When does three days start?

00:58:37.060 --> 00:58:38.490
When would you think it would start?

00:58:38.490 --> 00:58:40.850
- Like the moment you
get to the hotel, right?

00:58:40.850 --> 00:58:42.507
- That's day zero.
- That's day zero.

00:58:42.507 --> 00:58:44.757
But, here's the thing.
- That's orientation.

00:58:45.750 --> 00:58:47.220
- At every single checkpoint,

00:58:47.220 --> 00:58:50.630
I asked people which day does it start?

00:58:50.630 --> 00:58:52.230
And everyone said a different thing.

00:58:52.230 --> 00:58:56.040
So, I didn't know how long
I'm staying in this hotel for

00:58:56.040 --> 00:58:59.187
until I heard that thing where she says,

00:58:59.187 --> 00:59:01.670
"Hey, you will get a test on this day,

00:59:01.670 --> 00:59:02.677
and then if it's a
negative, you can leave."

00:59:02.677 --> 00:59:04.560
That is when I found out how long

00:59:04.560 --> 00:59:06.070
I'm staying in this hotel for.

00:59:06.070 --> 00:59:08.127
And yeah, so, if you get a
negative test, you can leave.

00:59:08.127 --> 00:59:10.420
But yeah, oh my God, it
was fucking terrible,

00:59:10.420 --> 00:59:11.480
just getting there.

00:59:11.480 --> 00:59:13.530
Not even to mention the hotel, oh my God.

00:59:13.530 --> 00:59:15.410
- 'Cause what was your room like?

00:59:15.410 --> 00:59:16.820
- So, it's a nice room.

00:59:16.820 --> 00:59:18.760
And like APA hotels-
- You stayed

00:59:18.760 --> 00:59:20.690
in the APA hotel, right?
- Yeah, did you not?

00:59:20.690 --> 00:59:22.150
- I didn't stay in APA hotel.

00:59:22.150 --> 00:59:25.960
- APA hotel is a chain of business hotels.

00:59:25.960 --> 00:59:28.760
Also very famous for having
a very funny book in them.

00:59:28.760 --> 00:59:30.370
Have you heard of this book?

00:59:30.370 --> 00:59:34.053
It's a revisionist book
of Japanese history,

00:59:35.630 --> 00:59:37.533
that is quite,

00:59:38.420 --> 00:59:39.253
what's the word?

00:59:39.253 --> 00:59:40.230
Racist, that's the word.

00:59:42.257 --> 00:59:43.750
It was a really famous book

00:59:43.750 --> 00:59:46.580
and it caused a lot of
controversy before the Olympics.

00:59:46.580 --> 00:59:50.070
Like the Chinese team
refused to stay in the hotel

00:59:50.070 --> 00:59:50.903
because of this book.

00:59:50.903 --> 00:59:52.280
- Oh yeah , I heard about that.

00:59:52.280 --> 00:59:54.490
- 'Cause this book, it
would say that like things

00:59:54.490 --> 00:59:57.110
that Japan did never
happened and stuff like that.

00:59:58.200 --> 00:59:59.870
It's kind of a somewhat
weird controversial,

00:59:59.870 --> 01:00:01.390
and the owner is a controversial figure

01:00:01.390 --> 01:00:02.920
of APA hotel, I think, as well.

01:00:02.920 --> 01:00:05.830
Anyway, just a fun little history.

01:00:05.830 --> 01:00:08.830
So this hotel, I had one of the rooms

01:00:08.830 --> 01:00:11.340
and it's just a business hotel.

01:00:11.340 --> 01:00:13.230
So you're not supposed
to be in there all day.

01:00:13.230 --> 01:00:14.670
The idea is that you go,

01:00:14.670 --> 01:00:16.470
you travel to like somewhere in Japan,

01:00:16.470 --> 01:00:18.710
you do your businesses in the
day and then you sleep there.

01:00:18.710 --> 01:00:20.216
- It's just used to shower and sleep

01:00:20.216 --> 01:00:21.217
- It's got everything you need.

01:00:21.217 --> 01:00:23.810
- I've stayed in the APA hotel as well.

01:00:23.810 --> 01:00:26.250
Probably like they're
all very similar style.

01:00:26.250 --> 01:00:27.960
I remember like there's
only enough space in there,

01:00:27.960 --> 01:00:29.837
for a bed.

01:00:29.837 --> 01:00:32.920
And there's no room to walk at all.

01:00:32.920 --> 01:00:35.870
It is very much like a prison cell.

01:00:35.870 --> 01:00:38.550
Because you do have a
TV, but the TV is like,

01:00:38.550 --> 01:00:40.070
you can probably kick the TV,

01:00:40.070 --> 01:00:41.577
with how close it is to the bed,

01:00:41.577 --> 01:00:44.850
'cause it's like, it has like enough space

01:00:44.850 --> 01:00:46.979
to contain a human being in it.

01:00:46.979 --> 01:00:47.812
- And that's what it's designed for.

01:00:47.812 --> 01:00:48.707
- Yeah, so I'm 5'10,

01:00:48.707 --> 01:00:50.480
and my feet were just
at the end of the bed.

01:00:50.480 --> 01:00:54.333
So if you were like
6'5, bro, you're fucked.

01:00:56.734 --> 01:00:58.710
And I show it off in the
video a lot, that I filmed,

01:00:58.710 --> 01:01:01.760
but you get this room,

01:01:01.760 --> 01:01:05.230
and there's about two steps horizontally

01:01:05.230 --> 01:01:07.740
and like two steps vertical
of walking the room.

01:01:07.740 --> 01:01:09.240
So that's all the room you have.

01:01:09.240 --> 01:01:12.060
You're not allowed to
leave the room, obviously.

01:01:12.060 --> 01:01:13.160
And if you do try and leave the room,

01:01:13.160 --> 01:01:15.650
there's an armed guard
outside who will shout at you

01:01:15.650 --> 01:01:16.600
if you even opened your door

01:01:16.600 --> 01:01:18.860
for longer than like five seconds.

01:01:18.860 --> 01:01:20.640
'Cause I spoke to an
Irish guy who was there

01:01:20.640 --> 01:01:22.113
and he said he wanted to get
some fresh air in his room

01:01:22.113 --> 01:01:24.050
because you can't open the window.

01:01:24.050 --> 01:01:26.040
You can't even crack it open.

01:01:26.040 --> 01:01:27.860
The window doesn't open at all.

01:01:27.860 --> 01:01:30.940
So if you want any fresh
air, like you can't.

01:01:30.940 --> 01:01:34.190
So it's kind of, at
least by the second day,

01:01:34.190 --> 01:01:36.540
my room started to smell not good.

01:01:36.540 --> 01:01:39.300
And so I understand that he
wanted to leave his door open,

01:01:39.300 --> 01:01:41.640
apparently like two guards came over

01:01:41.640 --> 01:01:43.120
and like told him to close the door.

01:01:43.120 --> 01:01:44.979
And if you do it again they'll like...

01:01:44.979 --> 01:01:47.734
(group chattering)

01:01:47.734 --> 01:01:49.434
- And then we never saw him again.

01:01:51.740 --> 01:01:53.760
- And now, so you spend
three days in that, right?

01:01:53.760 --> 01:01:56.160
If you get a negative
test, you get to leave.

01:01:56.160 --> 01:01:58.440
The scary thing was,
is the moment I landed

01:01:58.440 --> 01:02:00.450
and I got into my hotel, I got an email

01:02:00.450 --> 01:02:01.920
from the Ministry of Health,

01:02:01.920 --> 01:02:03.880
telling me that somebody on my flight

01:02:03.880 --> 01:02:06.440
tested positive for COVID.
- Oh shit!

01:02:06.440 --> 01:02:07.903
- So if I got COVID,

01:02:07.903 --> 01:02:11.640
I would have to stay in
that hotel for 14 days.

01:02:11.640 --> 01:02:13.700
So I don't know when
they change your sheets

01:02:13.700 --> 01:02:15.410
or do anything like that.

01:02:15.410 --> 01:02:16.730
- They don't change your sheets.

01:02:16.730 --> 01:02:19.270
- But I was accumulating a lot of trash,

01:02:19.270 --> 01:02:21.091
I mean, meals and stuff adds up,

01:02:21.091 --> 01:02:22.502
and the bottles and stuff adds up.

01:02:22.502 --> 01:02:23.335
- Wait, couldn't you get rid of that?

01:02:23.335 --> 01:02:26.203
- No, only the meal, they
didn't collect bottles.

01:02:27.210 --> 01:02:28.070
They took yours?

01:02:28.070 --> 01:02:29.960
Oh my God!
- We'll get into that.

01:02:29.960 --> 01:02:31.600
We'll get into that.

01:02:31.600 --> 01:02:33.790
- Okay, the room itself is nice.

01:02:33.790 --> 01:02:35.310
It's a good hotel except the pillow.

01:02:35.310 --> 01:02:37.176
The pillow, oh my God.

01:02:37.176 --> 01:02:40.800
This pillow is for sadists.

01:02:40.800 --> 01:02:44.030
It's one of those
concaved-like medical pillows.

01:02:44.030 --> 01:02:46.190
So your neck is like this,

01:02:46.190 --> 01:02:48.490
'cause it's supposed to
stretch your neck out.

01:02:49.570 --> 01:02:52.070
I do not wanna sleep on
that when I have jet lag

01:02:52.070 --> 01:02:53.370
and I'm trying to just fight for my life

01:02:53.370 --> 01:02:54.870
to get eight hours of sleep here.

01:02:54.870 --> 01:02:56.487
And so I told Garnt, I was like,

01:02:56.487 --> 01:02:59.760
"Bring your own pillow
because this pillows suck!"

01:02:59.760 --> 01:03:01.120
But you didn't have APA hotel,

01:03:01.120 --> 01:03:02.190
so I guess you didn't need it.

01:03:02.190 --> 01:03:04.520
But yeah, definitely the worst thing was

01:03:04.520 --> 01:03:06.750
not being able to walk or have fresh air.

01:03:06.750 --> 01:03:09.780
And I thought, "Okay,
at least even in prison,

01:03:09.780 --> 01:03:12.128
they get one hour of outside time of day.

01:03:12.128 --> 01:03:14.220
Can I have one hour of
outside time please?

01:03:14.220 --> 01:03:15.640
I want some walking."

01:03:15.640 --> 01:03:17.870
But it's only three days, so it's not bad.

01:03:17.870 --> 01:03:20.558
It was shit, but it had to be done.

01:03:20.558 --> 01:03:21.890
- And then the meals were crap, right?

01:03:21.890 --> 01:03:23.160
You guys sent me pictures of the meals.

01:03:23.160 --> 01:03:24.170
- Yeah, yeah.

01:03:24.170 --> 01:03:25.297
I posted one of them and I was like,

01:03:25.297 --> 01:03:26.770
"This is the saddest breakfast ever."

01:03:26.770 --> 01:03:29.730
And it caused a fucking
argument on Twitter.

01:03:29.730 --> 01:03:31.320
- You must have got canceled
on Twitter for that,

01:03:31.320 --> 01:03:32.153
didn't you?

01:03:32.153 --> 01:03:33.990
- Everyone was like, people
like, man, Connor's privileges,

01:03:33.990 --> 01:03:35.957
acting out so much...

01:03:35.957 --> 01:03:38.567
- Didn't you say something
like, "I don't eat breakfast."

01:03:38.567 --> 01:03:39.463
or something.

01:03:39.463 --> 01:03:40.646
- I don't eat breakfast.

01:03:40.646 --> 01:03:44.640
And this breakfast had like
French fries, slice tamps,

01:03:44.640 --> 01:03:45.640
which is fine but...

01:03:47.050 --> 01:03:50.240
There's single cheese
slices, sliced in half,

01:03:50.240 --> 01:03:53.380
one small tomato, one piece of broccoli,

01:03:53.380 --> 01:03:55.887
(indistinct) omelet, I still
didn't know what it was,

01:03:56.820 --> 01:03:59.700
a really, really hard croissant bread roll

01:03:59.700 --> 01:04:00.670
and cinnamon roll,

01:04:00.670 --> 01:04:03.123
and three pieces of
macaronI for breakfast.

01:04:03.123 --> 01:04:05.503
- I think in-flight meals
are better than that.

01:04:05.503 --> 01:04:06.527
- Well, that's the thing
is that, people were like,

01:04:06.527 --> 01:04:07.700
"This looks amazing."

01:04:07.700 --> 01:04:08.720
I'm like, "Think about it.

01:04:08.720 --> 01:04:09.620
This is breakfast.

01:04:09.620 --> 01:04:11.563
I just want cornflakes or something.

01:04:12.565 --> 01:04:13.415
I don't want this shit.

01:04:13.415 --> 01:04:14.248
What is this?

01:04:14.248 --> 01:04:15.620
I don't want cold french fries.

01:04:15.620 --> 01:04:18.010
That's another thing, all
of this stuff was very cold.

01:04:18.010 --> 01:04:19.250
- All the meals you get are cold.

01:04:19.250 --> 01:04:22.290
- Cold and they are-
- You don't have a microwave.

01:04:22.290 --> 01:04:23.280
- There's no way to heat it up.

01:04:23.280 --> 01:04:24.470
It would've been nice to have a microwave

01:04:24.470 --> 01:04:25.303
so I could heat them up.

01:04:25.303 --> 01:04:26.260
'Cause some of them are nice.

01:04:26.260 --> 01:04:28.610
There was one where they
made jerk chicken rice.

01:04:28.610 --> 01:04:29.790
And that was good.

01:04:29.790 --> 01:04:33.980
But most of them were really
ice cold, not that good.

01:04:33.980 --> 01:04:36.620
But that one breakfast, oh my God,

01:04:36.620 --> 01:04:37.930
that made me so depressed.

01:04:37.930 --> 01:04:39.920
I was like, "This is it?"

01:04:39.920 --> 01:04:41.970
- As if your situation
isn't already depressing.

01:04:41.970 --> 01:04:43.657
- And everyone was like,
"You're so privileged Connor."

01:04:43.657 --> 01:04:44.800
I'm like, "Look at it.

01:04:44.800 --> 01:04:47.750
This is not a balanced
breakfast in any capacity.

01:04:47.750 --> 01:04:50.610
No one should have cold
french fries for breakfast."

01:04:50.610 --> 01:04:51.860
I was like, "What's wrong with you guys?"

01:04:51.860 --> 01:04:52.693
'Cause they were like,

01:04:52.693 --> 01:04:53.950
"In my country, that would be amazing."

01:04:53.950 --> 01:04:55.260
I'm like, "What country?

01:04:55.260 --> 01:04:56.537
Tell me your country."

01:04:58.920 --> 01:05:01.503
(all laughing)

01:05:02.350 --> 01:05:03.960
Whenever I've been to countries

01:05:03.960 --> 01:05:07.600
that are not as wealthy
as other countries,

01:05:07.600 --> 01:05:09.510
they normally have the best breakfasts.

01:05:09.510 --> 01:05:11.330
'Cause they're always home
cooked and they're amazing

01:05:11.330 --> 01:05:13.680
and they're like really
cheap, really filling.

01:05:13.680 --> 01:05:14.890
I had Sri Lankan breakfast,

01:05:14.890 --> 01:05:16.987
that shit was the best shit
I'd ever had for breakfast.

01:05:16.987 --> 01:05:17.930
It was like a curry thing.

01:05:17.930 --> 01:05:18.810
I would kill for that

01:05:18.810 --> 01:05:20.510
over some shitty cornflakes or oatmeal.

01:05:20.510 --> 01:05:21.343
Are you kidding me?

01:05:21.343 --> 01:05:22.650
I got so annoyed about this whole thing.

01:05:22.650 --> 01:05:24.020
And everyone who called me privileged.

01:05:24.020 --> 01:05:27.640
- Well, it sounds like Garnt
had a much better time.

01:05:27.640 --> 01:05:29.110
- So like I was prepared...

01:05:29.110 --> 01:05:30.613
I was prepared for prison.

01:05:31.532 --> 01:05:34.220
'Cause I talked to other
people who'd traveled before

01:05:34.220 --> 01:05:37.520
and they had a very, very
similar experience to Connor,

01:05:37.520 --> 01:05:40.570
where you did feel like you
were stuck in a prison cage,

01:05:40.570 --> 01:05:42.220
and you couldn't leave your room.

01:05:43.060 --> 01:05:45.147
I knew about the cold meals as well.

01:05:45.147 --> 01:05:47.190
And like the one advice everyone gave me

