01:16:16.960 --> 01:16:19.520
We got like a pretty--
- Yeah, I saw your food,

01:16:19.520 --> 01:16:20.710
it looked way better than mine.

01:16:20.710 --> 01:16:23.683
- Yeah, we got like a fucking
decent bento everyday.

01:16:25.123 --> 01:16:27.113
Some of this shit was better than Matsiya.

01:16:29.610 --> 01:16:32.803
What was like the water
situation in your place?

01:16:33.710 --> 01:16:35.230
- So you can ask for
more bottles of water.

01:16:35.230 --> 01:16:38.680
A unit got one bottle of
water with every meal.

01:16:38.680 --> 01:16:41.040
And I ran out 'cause I was a thirsty boy.

01:16:41.040 --> 01:16:42.187
And I asked for more and they said,

01:16:42.187 --> 01:16:43.120
"Oh, sure, we'll deliver it."

01:16:43.120 --> 01:16:43.953
They never delivered it.

01:16:43.953 --> 01:16:45.533
They just didn't turn up.

01:16:46.606 --> 01:16:47.439
- So when we went in...

01:16:47.439 --> 01:16:49.040
Oh, sorry, I forgot to say,

01:16:49.040 --> 01:16:51.140
our place also had a minI fridge as well.

01:16:51.140 --> 01:16:53.589
- Ah, mine did as well.
- Did yours as well?

01:16:53.589 --> 01:16:54.422
- I think most hotels have minI fridges.

01:16:54.422 --> 01:16:56.690
- It just like never got cold though.

01:16:56.690 --> 01:16:59.370
It was just like--
- Just a container.

01:16:59.370 --> 01:17:01.450
- They made it like less
than room temperature,

01:17:01.450 --> 01:17:03.210
which I was like, I guess that's good.

01:17:03.210 --> 01:17:04.620
But like, I mean, what am I gonna do,

01:17:04.620 --> 01:17:07.060
call them and make them
replace the fridge?

01:17:07.060 --> 01:17:09.860
- So we realized water would
be a very important resource

01:17:09.860 --> 01:17:11.320
to fucking survive as it is.

01:17:11.320 --> 01:17:13.963
They said you can use tap
water, but you know, obviously.

01:17:15.028 --> 01:17:17.980
- It taste like shit in Japan.
- Yeah, it does.

01:17:17.980 --> 01:17:20.720
So we go in and there
is two bottles of water,

01:17:20.720 --> 01:17:22.920
which is standard, I guess,
for every hotel stay.

01:17:22.920 --> 01:17:23.970
- I didn't even know that.

01:17:23.970 --> 01:17:24.803
- You didn't?
- No.

01:17:24.803 --> 01:17:26.290
- Okay, so they gave us..

01:17:26.290 --> 01:17:28.760
They started off with two bottles of water

01:17:28.760 --> 01:17:30.060
and then we opened the mini fridge

01:17:30.060 --> 01:17:32.360
and it was a mini fridge
full of bottles of water.

01:17:32.360 --> 01:17:34.440
- Oh, fuck off.
(Garnt laughing)

01:17:34.440 --> 01:17:35.687
Mine wasn't even on.

01:17:35.687 --> 01:17:36.761
I had to turn it on.

01:17:36.761 --> 01:17:38.780
- So at the start of our journey,

01:17:38.780 --> 01:17:41.630
we had like eight bottles of
water, which is brilliant.

01:17:41.630 --> 01:17:43.540
And every time they delivered meals,

01:17:43.540 --> 01:17:45.700
which was like three times a day,

01:17:45.700 --> 01:17:48.620
which was like, they gave
us more food than I needed

01:17:48.620 --> 01:17:50.310
because by the time...

01:17:50.310 --> 01:17:52.270
I had the breakfast was massive

01:17:52.270 --> 01:17:53.660
and by the time lunch
was being delivered--

01:17:53.660 --> 01:17:54.906
- I often didn't eat breakfast

01:17:54.906 --> 01:17:55.860
'cause I just wasn't hungry at breakfast.

01:17:55.860 --> 01:17:57.370
- Yeah, by the time lunch was delivered,

01:17:57.370 --> 01:17:59.210
I was still full from breakfast.

01:17:59.210 --> 01:18:00.480
So I had a little bit of lunch.

01:18:00.480 --> 01:18:01.860
And then like, by the time dinner came,

01:18:01.860 --> 01:18:04.430
I was eating like a king.

01:18:04.430 --> 01:18:05.319
I don't know.

01:18:05.319 --> 01:18:07.490
- This man, this man, this man.

01:18:07.490 --> 01:18:08.323
- It was a great experience.

01:18:08.323 --> 01:18:09.650
- The dichotomy that we faced, oh my gosh.

01:18:09.650 --> 01:18:13.020
- This guy is literally
living like a English king

01:18:13.020 --> 01:18:14.350
during the black plague.

01:18:14.350 --> 01:18:16.500
- Yeah, this man is a plague-

01:18:16.500 --> 01:18:18.820
- While the peasants are
dying from the black plague

01:18:18.820 --> 01:18:19.653
he's just like,

01:18:19.653 --> 01:18:22.070
"Oh, there's too much
food here guys, fuck me"

01:18:22.070 --> 01:18:24.801
- It's like, you know
that scene in Goodfellas

01:18:24.801 --> 01:18:26.020
well the gangsters like go to jail,

01:18:26.020 --> 01:18:28.949
but they're having-
- They're like champagne

01:18:28.949 --> 01:18:30.481
- Like champagne and shit.

01:18:30.481 --> 01:18:34.080
That's basically my
quarantine hotel experience.

01:18:34.080 --> 01:18:35.230
I didn't wanna leave, honestly.

01:18:35.230 --> 01:18:38.390
Me and Sydney woke up on the third day

01:18:38.390 --> 01:18:40.638
and we're like, oh, do we have to go now?

01:18:40.638 --> 01:18:41.959
Do we have to go back to our--

01:18:41.959 --> 01:18:43.157
- Can one of us just get COVID?

01:18:43.157 --> 01:18:44.340
(all laughing)
Just so we stay here

01:18:44.340 --> 01:18:46.033
for like two weeks or so.

01:18:46.033 --> 01:18:48.110
- It was just a free vacation.

01:18:48.110 --> 01:18:49.577
I didn't have enough to pay for it,

01:18:49.577 --> 01:18:50.510
didn't have enough to pay for the meals.

01:18:50.510 --> 01:18:52.050
It was a good meal everyday,

01:18:52.050 --> 01:18:53.960
had a hotel service.

01:18:53.960 --> 01:18:55.550
- While this man living in the slums.

01:18:55.550 --> 01:18:56.420
- Fucking great.

01:18:56.420 --> 01:18:58.460
- Well, I got so depressed.

01:18:58.460 --> 01:19:01.363
Like on the second, third
day I was miserable.

01:19:02.382 --> 01:19:03.215
What's it called?

01:19:03.215 --> 01:19:04.880
Cabin fever, is that what it is?

01:19:05.780 --> 01:19:08.330
I couldn't even play games or watch shit,

01:19:08.330 --> 01:19:10.280
'cause I was just so miserable.

01:19:10.280 --> 01:19:11.580
- You were just like lying in bed?

01:19:11.580 --> 01:19:13.900
- I was just like lying
there, checking Twitter

01:19:13.900 --> 01:19:15.680
then just like, should I do something?

01:19:15.680 --> 01:19:16.520
No, I'm too tired.

01:19:16.520 --> 01:19:17.353
Why?

01:19:17.353 --> 01:19:18.186
'Cause I can't fucking walk.

01:19:18.186 --> 01:19:20.380
So I'm literally just
lying, sitting down all day.

01:19:20.380 --> 01:19:21.330
- You're just bed-ridden.

01:19:21.330 --> 01:19:23.510
- Yeah, and it make you feel fucking awful

01:19:23.510 --> 01:19:24.810
I don't know, if it was terrible.

01:19:24.810 --> 01:19:25.797
I know I'm gonna sound
just like a little bitch,

01:19:25.797 --> 01:19:28.140
and I'm sure everyone's gonna say that.

01:19:28.140 --> 01:19:30.390
- I saw the photos, some
of the photos you sent.

01:19:30.390 --> 01:19:31.610
- I'd feel the same way.

01:19:31.610 --> 01:19:33.530
- It's one of those things where
when you see it and hear it

01:19:33.530 --> 01:19:34.660
you're like doesn't sound too bad

01:19:34.660 --> 01:19:36.297
but then when you do it you're like,

01:19:36.297 --> 01:19:38.720
"Oh, shit this is really depressing."

01:19:38.720 --> 01:19:40.990
- Meanwhile me and Sydney
were just like playing games

01:19:40.990 --> 01:19:42.730
on like the big screen
TV in the living room

01:19:42.730 --> 01:19:44.757
and I'm just like it's fucking brilliant.

01:19:44.757 --> 01:19:45.590
I'm like--

01:19:45.590 --> 01:19:47.663
- Let's pull out the PS5 we packed in.

01:19:47.663 --> 01:19:49.700
- I didn't have a game console.

01:19:49.700 --> 01:19:51.960
I tried playing some games on my laptop

01:19:51.960 --> 01:19:52.980
but I immediately was like,

01:19:52.980 --> 01:19:54.660
oh, this shit is not comfortable.

01:19:54.660 --> 01:19:56.936
It's not comfortable doing this.

01:19:56.936 --> 01:19:59.277
And the smell of my
room was so goddamn bad,

01:19:59.277 --> 01:20:00.790
'cause all the food.

01:20:00.790 --> 01:20:03.210
It was like coagulating in the air

01:20:03.210 --> 01:20:04.500
and my sweat.

01:20:04.500 --> 01:20:06.500
- But then after reading a few more posts

01:20:06.500 --> 01:20:09.070
and after like talking to various people

01:20:09.070 --> 01:20:12.200
I think your hotel quality experience

01:20:12.200 --> 01:20:14.240
is literally down to chance.

01:20:14.240 --> 01:20:16.340
- Well, yeah, 'cause there's three buses.

01:20:16.340 --> 01:20:17.840
I noticed there's three bus lines

01:20:17.840 --> 01:20:19.980
and they all take you
to a different hotel.

01:20:19.980 --> 01:20:22.300
And whichever one you go to,
you get a different experience.

01:20:22.300 --> 01:20:24.850
- I think our hotel was
not just a business hotel

01:20:24.850 --> 01:20:27.380
it was actually like a four-star hotel,

01:20:27.380 --> 01:20:28.430
where they put us in.

01:20:28.430 --> 01:20:29.680
- Certainly sounds like it.

01:20:29.680 --> 01:20:31.250
- Yeah, which I'm just like,

01:20:32.110 --> 01:20:34.800
Gacha luck man, the Gacha
lords are on your side.

01:20:34.800 --> 01:20:35.900
- You know I will say,

01:20:37.069 --> 01:20:39.020
this is kind of...

01:20:39.020 --> 01:20:41.616
Don't make any more Squid
Game jokes but this is...

01:20:41.616 --> 01:20:44.530
When I got on the bus that we all came on

01:20:44.530 --> 01:20:47.000
there was like half the people on the bus,

01:20:47.000 --> 01:20:49.151
which means that half of them got COVID.

01:20:49.151 --> 01:20:50.040
(Joey laughing)

01:20:50.040 --> 01:20:50.873
- [Garnt] Fucking hell.

01:20:50.873 --> 01:20:53.270
- It was weird.
- First round elimination

01:20:53.270 --> 01:20:54.647
- The Irish guy was there who I spoke to

01:20:54.647 --> 01:20:55.750
and the old man was there.

01:20:55.750 --> 01:20:57.461
So I was like...

01:20:57.461 --> 01:21:00.044
(all laughing)

01:21:01.560 --> 01:21:03.202
- What's up guys?

01:21:03.202 --> 01:21:06.119
(group chattering)

01:21:07.720 --> 01:21:09.620
- So I saw that guy without his mask on

01:21:09.620 --> 01:21:11.647
in front of like seven armed
guards, not giving a fuck,

01:21:11.647 --> 01:21:14.400
and I was like damn man, I did it.

01:21:14.400 --> 01:21:16.350
- What day did you travel on?

01:21:16.350 --> 01:21:17.973
- What date?
- What day?

01:21:19.390 --> 01:21:20.223
- What do you mean like?

01:21:20.223 --> 01:21:22.170
- Was it like a Saturday like a Friday?

01:21:22.170 --> 01:21:23.003
- I don't know man, it was all the same,

01:21:23.003 --> 01:21:24.310
it was all the same.

01:21:24.310 --> 01:21:26.297
- 'Cause what I will say is that

01:21:28.428 --> 01:21:29.890
I traveled on like a weekday

01:21:29.890 --> 01:21:31.270
so like not many people were traveling

01:21:31.270 --> 01:21:32.320
so I feel like...

01:21:32.320 --> 01:21:33.370
I was traveling on a,

01:21:34.690 --> 01:21:36.430
Friday maybe, I don't know.

01:21:36.430 --> 01:21:38.010
- I mean, yeah, Friday's like a peak time

01:21:38.010 --> 01:21:38.843
for people who are traveling

01:21:38.843 --> 01:21:41.871
- I'm not sure you know,
I have to have a look.

01:21:41.871 --> 01:21:42.890
- 'Cause if you travel on the weekend

01:21:42.890 --> 01:21:44.420
I think more people travel on the weekend

01:21:44.420 --> 01:21:48.130
'cause I feel like the
worst hotels are for like,

01:21:48.130 --> 01:21:49.985
when there are too many people traveling

01:21:49.985 --> 01:21:51.420
that it kind of like bleeds out.

01:21:51.420 --> 01:21:56.420
Because, I think we didn't
have too many buses.

01:21:56.470 --> 01:21:59.580
Which is why like, I think
we had like one or two buses,

01:21:59.580 --> 01:22:01.836
and they all went to the same place.

01:22:01.836 --> 01:22:05.100
So I feel like once that hotel
started getting filled out,

01:22:05.100 --> 01:22:06.230
I mean if you think about it,

01:22:06.230 --> 01:22:08.880
why would you need to drive
one and a half hours...

01:22:08.880 --> 01:22:12.730
'Cause we flew in through
Haneda which is like south.

01:22:12.730 --> 01:22:15.590
There's no reason to drive
to a hotel in the north.

01:22:15.590 --> 01:22:16.650
- Well they drove to the hotel

01:22:16.650 --> 01:22:18.400
and they drove us back to the airport.

01:22:18.400 --> 01:22:19.760
And then when you get to the airport

01:22:19.760 --> 01:22:24.760
you have to have a weird specific taxi.

01:22:25.080 --> 01:22:26.370
You can't get a normal taxi,

01:22:26.370 --> 01:22:27.680
can't book a normal taxi,

01:22:27.680 --> 01:22:29.783
it has to be a quarantine approved taxi.

01:22:31.150 --> 01:22:32.450
And the problem is that

01:22:32.450 --> 01:22:34.510
I didn't know what time we were leaving.

01:22:34.510 --> 01:22:37.090
So what time I should I tell this taxi?

01:22:37.090 --> 01:22:38.340
I couldn't figure it out.

01:22:38.340 --> 01:22:39.173
So I didn't know.

01:22:39.173 --> 01:22:41.470
So I had to guess and I
had to wait for two hours

01:22:41.470 --> 01:22:42.340
at the Haneda.

01:22:42.340 --> 01:22:43.770
But the thing was, right,

01:22:43.770 --> 01:22:46.610
so this whole period has
just been in quarantine.

01:22:46.610 --> 01:22:49.403
They drop you off at Haneda,
and they're like, fuck off.

01:22:50.370 --> 01:22:51.860
No one checks you.

01:22:51.860 --> 01:22:53.730
No one makes sure and
everyone just went went off.

01:22:53.730 --> 01:22:55.272
And I was like, where's everyone going?

01:22:55.272 --> 01:22:57.170
Does everyone know where they're going?

01:22:57.170 --> 01:23:00.250
I spoke to the Irish guy
who'd done it a few times

01:23:00.250 --> 01:23:01.083
and he was like,

01:23:01.083 --> 01:23:02.920
"Yeah, you can just chill
around the airport and wait."

01:23:02.920 --> 01:23:05.480
I'm like, well I can just go to the cafe

01:23:05.480 --> 01:23:06.630
and interact with people.

01:23:06.630 --> 01:23:07.670
He's like, "Yeah, if you want to."

01:23:07.670 --> 01:23:09.150
And I'm like, that doesn't seem right.

01:23:09.150 --> 01:23:11.417
I didn't, I just I stood
in like a corner waiting

01:23:11.417 --> 01:23:13.670
far away from everyone, and I
was like don't come near me,

01:23:13.670 --> 01:23:14.503
I'm sick.

01:23:16.170 --> 01:23:18.390
But I mean, yeah, it was fucking weird

01:23:18.390 --> 01:23:19.223
and it was--

01:23:19.223 --> 01:23:20.370
- You're literally like that dude

01:23:20.370 --> 01:23:21.720
who's been in jail for most of their life

01:23:21.720 --> 01:23:24.552
just trying to assimilate
back into society.

01:23:24.552 --> 01:23:28.241
(group chattering)

01:23:28.241 --> 01:23:30.460
- Yeah man, it was it was fucking weird

01:23:30.460 --> 01:23:32.650
and not a very fun experience

01:23:32.650 --> 01:23:35.140
and they've got rid of
it now, for UK travelers.

01:23:35.140 --> 01:23:35.973
- Oh, really?

01:23:35.973 --> 01:23:38.570
- Have they got rid of it, have they?

01:23:38.570 --> 01:23:39.970
- They probably will soon.

01:23:39.970 --> 01:23:41.140
- They reduced the quarantine time.

01:23:41.140 --> 01:23:42.373
Before we flew,

01:23:43.250 --> 01:23:44.710
I mean before we flew off to England,

01:23:44.710 --> 01:23:46.177
it was six days in quarantine hotel

01:23:46.177 --> 01:23:49.440
and then they got halved to
three days in quarantine.

01:23:49.440 --> 01:23:52.590
- Six days in a hotel, fuck!

01:23:52.590 --> 01:23:56.280
- Why couldn't be six days?
- He would've been all right.

01:23:56.280 --> 01:23:58.630
- I shiver at the thought of
spending another day there.

01:23:58.630 --> 01:24:01.330
It was nerve wracking, 'cause
the day I had to do my test,

01:24:01.330 --> 01:24:02.257
they called me up and they said,

01:24:02.257 --> 01:24:05.260
"Hey, when you get your
results if they're negative

01:24:05.260 --> 01:24:07.440
you have to leave the room right away.

01:24:07.440 --> 01:24:11.543
So you have to pack just in
case that you're leaving.

01:24:12.550 --> 01:24:13.530
- But I didn't know

01:24:13.530 --> 01:24:15.700
'cause someone on my
plane had been infected

01:24:15.700 --> 01:24:18.510
there's a good chance
that I could have got it.

01:24:18.510 --> 01:24:20.277
Luckily I didn't but
like they called me up,

01:24:20.277 --> 01:24:21.200
they're like, "Your test
results are negative,

01:24:21.200 --> 01:24:23.270
please leave the room
as soon as possible."

01:24:23.270 --> 01:24:24.331
And like everyone's leaving.

01:24:24.331 --> 01:24:26.180
And I was like, what the fuck,
I gotta get out of the room.

01:24:26.180 --> 01:24:28.870
Which is weird, it was
really a shit experience,

01:24:28.870 --> 01:24:31.600
don't recommend, IGN
is 10 out of 10 there.

01:24:31.600 --> 01:24:34.100
- I wouldn't recommend that experience,

01:24:34.100 --> 01:24:35.360
my experience wasn't that bad.

01:24:35.360 --> 01:24:37.921
- Oh yeah, you got a free suite hotel.

01:24:37.921 --> 01:24:40.271
- I remember Connor like
messaging me every day

01:24:41.560 --> 01:24:45.190
Connor was like trying to drag
something negative out of me,

01:24:45.190 --> 01:24:46.886
and I'm just like,

01:24:46.886 --> 01:24:47.990
(group chattering)

01:24:47.990 --> 01:24:50.150
And he's like tell me about,
Garnt, tell me about it.

01:24:50.150 --> 01:24:52.770
I was like, honestly it's
just pretty good actually.

01:24:52.770 --> 01:24:54.023
I'm having a good time.

01:24:55.150 --> 01:24:56.810
He'd mention to me the
next day, me being like

01:24:56.810 --> 01:24:58.550
maybe this this day will get to him,

01:24:58.550 --> 01:24:59.383
this day will get to him.

01:24:59.383 --> 01:25:01.870
- I'm sure something
bad happened since then.

01:25:01.870 --> 01:25:04.030
- I went on Twitter as
well the day I checked in

01:25:04.030 --> 01:25:07.233
and a fucking video from
Zed, the musical artist.

01:25:08.480 --> 01:25:11.140
This motherfucker had like
a penthouse suite somewhere,

01:25:11.140 --> 01:25:13.220
like literally a penthouse suite.

01:25:13.220 --> 01:25:17.830
- [Zed] A bedroom and an insane view.

01:25:17.830 --> 01:25:20.803
Look at this, just crazy.

01:25:22.280 --> 01:25:25.470
I'm ready for the
quarantine, let's get it.

01:25:25.470 --> 01:25:26.790
- And bear in mind,

01:25:26.790 --> 01:25:29.620
Japan isn't even giving out
visas right now to anyone,

01:25:29.620 --> 01:25:31.277
but somehow he got in?

01:25:31.277 --> 01:25:32.680
- He got a penthouse suite in Japan.

01:25:32.680 --> 01:25:34.990
- In Japan and he got a
visa to get in, somehow,

01:25:34.990 --> 01:25:35.990
because he's doing a concert.

01:25:35.990 --> 01:25:37.500
And somehow they made an exception

01:25:37.500 --> 01:25:38.869
and people were not happy

01:25:38.869 --> 01:25:40.920
because there was tons of people
in the comments being like,

01:25:40.920 --> 01:25:43.240
Zed, you know that students
haven't been able to enter Japan

01:25:43.240 --> 01:25:44.877
in two years, what the fuck,

01:25:44.877 --> 01:25:46.940
and he's off here showing his suite.

01:25:46.940 --> 01:25:49.520
And Zed didn't even have to
do a quarantine for two weeks,

01:25:49.520 --> 01:25:50.593
only three days.

01:25:51.730 --> 01:25:53.220
- Yeah so after the quarantine hotel

01:25:53.220 --> 01:25:54.950
you still have to quarantine at home

01:25:54.950 --> 01:25:56.659
for two weeks.
- For 11 days.

01:25:56.659 --> 01:25:57.492
- For 11 days

01:25:57.492 --> 01:25:59.148
- There were people trying
to cancel you for privilege.

01:25:59.148 --> 01:26:01.040
- I was like--
- That's real privilege there.

01:26:01.040 --> 01:26:03.900
- I made a joke 'cause he gave a room tour

01:26:03.900 --> 01:26:05.460
that was like two minutes long,

01:26:05.460 --> 01:26:07.800
of like all the different rooms he had

01:26:07.800 --> 01:26:09.400
and all the shit he'd been sent.

01:26:09.400 --> 01:26:11.340
He'd been sent like
everything you'd ever need.

01:26:11.340 --> 01:26:14.057
Someone sent him like a
gaming pc for his quarantine

01:26:14.057 --> 01:26:16.670
and I was like this is fucking stupid.

01:26:16.670 --> 01:26:19.250
This is the stupidest shit I've ever seen.

01:26:19.250 --> 01:26:21.440
And I made a parody video.

01:26:21.440 --> 01:26:23.320
I was like, "Hey guys this is my room tour

01:26:23.320 --> 01:26:24.350
and I just turned the camera

01:26:24.350 --> 01:26:26.640
and it's just like the room
and that's the whole room.

01:26:26.640 --> 01:26:28.730
And I was just joking.

01:26:28.730 --> 01:26:31.210
I was just joking about how like,

01:26:31.210 --> 01:26:33.020
the difference compared to rooms.

01:26:33.020 --> 01:26:34.640
And then people got
angry at me being like,

01:26:34.640 --> 01:26:37.270
you should be happy that you
even were able to enter Japan.

01:26:37.270 --> 01:26:38.660
You know people haven't
been able to enter Japan

01:26:38.660 --> 01:26:40.430
for two years, the privilege your showing.

01:26:40.430 --> 01:26:42.630
I'm like what the fuck is this?

01:26:42.630 --> 01:26:43.960
What the fuck?

01:26:43.960 --> 01:26:44.921
I was so annoyed.

01:26:44.921 --> 01:26:45.754
- You just can't get a dove there.

01:26:45.754 --> 01:26:46.587
- So I deleted the tweet,

01:26:46.587 --> 01:26:47.990
I was getting pissed off with the replies.

01:26:47.990 --> 01:26:49.420
I was like what the
fuck are these reply...

01:26:49.420 --> 01:26:51.180
And they're like why are you blaming me?

01:26:51.180 --> 01:26:54.680
Don't blame me for being
a resident in a country

01:26:54.680 --> 01:26:55.760
and getting back in,

01:26:55.760 --> 01:26:58.700
blame the country for
banning any form of visas,

01:26:58.700 --> 01:26:59.850
what the fuck!
- Yeah, exactly.

01:26:59.850 --> 01:27:01.150
- They were like taking it out on me,

01:27:01.150 --> 01:27:02.400
I was getting so annoyed.

01:27:03.416 --> 01:27:04.249
I was fuming, fuming.

01:27:04.249 --> 01:27:05.390
- I mean, those people
couldn't fucking tweet

01:27:05.390 --> 01:27:06.310
to the Japanese government,

01:27:06.310 --> 01:27:08.588
so they had to go for the next best thing.

01:27:08.588 --> 01:27:09.421
- They were like,

01:27:09.421 --> 01:27:10.610
"You're so lucky that
you can re-enter Japan."

01:27:10.610 --> 01:27:12.930
Like, I'm lucky that i
can re-enter the country

01:27:12.930 --> 01:27:14.640
I fucking live in, what
the fuck do you mean?

01:27:14.640 --> 01:27:17.080
Shut the fuck up.
(Joey laughing)

01:27:17.080 --> 01:27:17.913
Like what?

01:27:17.913 --> 01:27:18.780
This is absurd.

01:27:18.780 --> 01:27:20.600
Don't try and say that I'm lucky.

01:27:20.600 --> 01:27:23.010
- That is pretty unfair.
- We're all unlucky

01:27:23.010 --> 01:27:25.120
that the government has
some shitty rules on this.

01:27:25.120 --> 01:27:27.400
Like don't don't take
it out on each other.

01:27:27.400 --> 01:27:28.750
That's why I got annoyed about it

01:27:28.750 --> 01:27:30.780
'cause people are attacking other people

01:27:30.780 --> 01:27:32.740
who are able to get into the country

01:27:32.740 --> 01:27:34.820
instead of, I don't
know, blaming the people

01:27:34.820 --> 01:27:35.830
who are making the rules

01:27:35.830 --> 01:27:38.160
and these arbitrary
rules between countries.

01:27:38.160 --> 01:27:42.410
Like in America, some
states have to quarantine

01:27:42.410 --> 01:27:43.600
but others don't.

01:27:43.600 --> 01:27:45.590
And so there's this
whole weird thing where

01:27:45.590 --> 01:27:48.443
it's like why, I mean it's
all one country, right?

01:27:49.721 --> 01:27:50.820
- I mean, same with Australia as well,

01:27:50.820 --> 01:27:52.860
like most of the states...

01:27:52.860 --> 01:27:55.140
Like I mean, Australia had
that the fucking worst though.

01:27:55.140 --> 01:27:57.137
Like, Victoria I think was in lock down

01:27:57.137 --> 01:27:59.580
for 280 days in a row,
something like that.

01:27:59.580 --> 01:28:01.690
Like, no interstate thing.

01:28:01.690 --> 01:28:02.523
My sister was like,

01:28:02.523 --> 01:28:05.000
yeah, I'm not allowed to
travel more than 10 kilometers

01:28:05.000 --> 01:28:06.850
from my house, otherwise I get fined.

01:28:06.850 --> 01:28:08.810
But like there's nothing stopping you

01:28:08.810 --> 01:28:10.690
from just, if you live in like...

01:28:10.690 --> 01:28:13.030
So one of the countries that
was banned was like Texas.

01:28:13.030 --> 01:28:15.080
You could just fly--
- You mean state?

01:28:15.080 --> 01:28:15.980
- Yeah, the state.

01:28:17.030 --> 01:28:19.470
- The country of Texas. (laughs)

01:28:19.470 --> 01:28:21.160
The state of Texas was like one country

01:28:21.160 --> 01:28:24.210
that you'd have to quarantine
in, go to the hotel for.

01:28:24.210 --> 01:28:25.043
But there were other states

01:28:25.043 --> 01:28:25.890
that you didn't have
to go to the hotel for.

01:28:25.890 --> 01:28:28.790
So like why wouldn't you just
drive over to the next state

01:28:28.790 --> 01:28:29.623
and fly from there?

01:28:29.623 --> 01:28:31.450
And just say that you've been there?

01:28:31.450 --> 01:28:33.330
Because there's no way
they can validate that.

01:28:33.330 --> 01:28:34.163
- They can check that, right?

01:28:34.163 --> 01:28:37.100
- So to me it just felt
really like fucking weird.

01:28:37.100 --> 01:28:39.500
But COVID has shown that

01:28:39.500 --> 01:28:41.990
the rules are not to do
with what's practical,

01:28:41.990 --> 01:28:44.670
it's political ties and all those things

01:28:44.670 --> 01:28:47.560
if we've learned anything
and that's what is shitty,

01:28:47.560 --> 01:28:49.430
is that it sometimes feels
like you're just caught up

01:28:49.430 --> 01:28:52.513
in some international
bullshit politics of countries

01:28:52.513 --> 01:28:53.970
that don't like each other

01:28:53.970 --> 01:28:56.850
and countries that do like
each other and favoring.

01:28:56.850 --> 01:28:58.970
I mean the UK did it a lot
too with countries as well.

01:28:58.970 --> 01:28:59.860
They've been pretty bad for it.

01:28:59.860 --> 01:29:02.580
It was just a mess and I
hated it and it's shit.

01:29:02.580 --> 01:29:04.850
- Well at least you guys got to you know

01:29:04.850 --> 01:29:07.003
sit here with me.
- Yeah, yeah.

01:29:09.030 --> 01:29:10.670
- You guys made it, you made it.

01:29:10.670 --> 01:29:12.960
- I mean like for the longest time we were

01:29:12.960 --> 01:29:14.320
like literally trapped in this country

01:29:14.320 --> 01:29:16.170
because we couldn't fly
out for the longest time.

01:29:16.170 --> 01:29:19.260
And it was only recently
that the rules got changed

01:29:19.260 --> 01:29:22.200
that people who are already
residents can fly out

01:29:22.200 --> 01:29:24.400
and then fly back in, you know.

01:29:24.400 --> 01:29:27.050
And I mean now we're just
waiting for the actual

01:29:27.050 --> 01:29:28.640
people who are waiting on visas

01:29:28.640 --> 01:29:32.280
because I can only imagine
that, that does suck.

01:29:32.280 --> 01:29:36.170
Because we were really lucky
to be able to get our visas

01:29:36.170 --> 01:29:37.550
before all this happened

01:29:37.550 --> 01:29:38.820
otherwise we would have literally,

01:29:38.820 --> 01:29:41.370
Trash Taste would have never happened,

01:29:41.370 --> 01:29:42.770
if we would had applied for our visas

01:29:42.770 --> 01:29:45.203
literally a few months
after we got our visas.

01:29:46.530 --> 01:29:48.360
We would still be waiting now

01:29:48.360 --> 01:29:50.130
to even get our visas to move to Japan.

01:29:50.130 --> 01:29:51.257
It's actually crazy to think about.

01:29:51.257 --> 01:29:52.870
- And Japan faced a lot of criticism

01:29:52.870 --> 01:29:55.200
when the coronavirus started

01:29:55.200 --> 01:29:57.730
'cause they banned...

01:29:57.730 --> 01:30:00.610
Only Japanese nationals
were allowed back in.

01:30:00.610 --> 01:30:02.380
Which is like okay I
guess that makes sense

01:30:02.380 --> 01:30:05.740
but then they also didn't
allow green card holders,

01:30:05.740 --> 01:30:08.190
permanent residents,
- Really?

01:30:08.190 --> 01:30:09.023
- Yeah.

01:30:11.761 --> 01:30:12.594
If you're like me you're British

01:30:12.594 --> 01:30:13.540
and you're married to a Japanese woman

01:30:13.540 --> 01:30:15.740
and then you went and
then you came back in,

01:30:17.210 --> 01:30:18.530
if I was married to Japanese person,

01:30:18.530 --> 01:30:20.973
they'd be allowed in but
I wouldn't be allowed in.

01:30:23.549 --> 01:30:25.500
That came under a shit ton of criticism,

01:30:25.500 --> 01:30:26.404
rightfully so,

01:30:26.404 --> 01:30:29.930
because if someone's a permanent
resident of your country

01:30:29.930 --> 01:30:31.967
that's literally like
where their whole life is.

01:30:31.967 --> 01:30:34.120
You can't just say like, no, but they did,

01:30:34.120 --> 01:30:35.240
and they faced a lot of criticism,

01:30:35.240 --> 01:30:36.860
which they did eventually change

01:30:36.860 --> 01:30:38.500
but they've still been banning visas.

01:30:38.500 --> 01:30:42.290
And like I feel really fucking
sorry for these students

01:30:42.290 --> 01:30:43.840
who've had their life on pause,

01:30:44.766 --> 01:30:48.020
who had their whole
like basically two years

01:30:48.020 --> 01:30:50.480
lined up in Japan,
they've just been banned

01:30:50.480 --> 01:30:52.980
from entering Japan.
- They've just been waiting.

01:30:53.830 --> 01:30:55.010
- It doesn't make sense to me

01:30:55.010 --> 01:30:56.600
that they wouldn't allow some system

01:30:56.600 --> 01:30:57.650
even if it's complicated

01:30:57.650 --> 01:30:59.760
and even if it's fucking
stupid and tedious

01:30:59.760 --> 01:31:01.260
to get in if you're a student.

01:31:01.260 --> 01:31:02.560
Like I don't understand

01:31:02.560 --> 01:31:04.880
why they haven't changed the rule on that.

01:31:04.880 --> 01:31:06.750
It's just Japan being Japan, you know.

01:31:06.750 --> 01:31:08.500
- Yeah it's because Japan thinks that,

01:31:08.500 --> 01:31:09.670
oh, the foreigners,

01:31:09.670 --> 01:31:11.810
you're more likely to get
it if you're a foreigner,

01:31:11.810 --> 01:31:13.340
which is just not true.

01:31:13.340 --> 01:31:16.170
- Yeah, it's just one
of those things where,

01:31:16.170 --> 01:31:19.160
you can go through enough precautions

01:31:19.160 --> 01:31:20.640
and you can do enough tests

01:31:20.640 --> 01:31:22.980
to make sure that 99% of
the time you'll get it,

01:31:22.980 --> 01:31:24.380
so that it's good and it works,

01:31:24.380 --> 01:31:25.930
but I don't know to me it just,

01:31:26.800 --> 01:31:28.520
I can't fathom it why they've banned

01:31:28.520 --> 01:31:30.400
issuing any visas at all.

01:31:30.400 --> 01:31:32.070
It really doesn't make sense to me.

01:31:32.070 --> 01:31:33.440
- Yeah, I don't know, it's dumb as fuck.

01:31:33.440 --> 01:31:35.540
- Yeah, and after going through that

01:31:35.540 --> 01:31:36.890
quarantine experience like,

01:31:37.770 --> 01:31:40.150
I don't believe anyone who's flying in

01:31:40.150 --> 01:31:41.930
is spreading COVID. (laughing)

01:31:41.930 --> 01:31:43.140
People, my God.

01:31:43.140 --> 01:31:45.420
They have this shit on lockdown man.

01:31:45.420 --> 01:31:46.850
- Yeah, honestly.

01:31:46.850 --> 01:31:48.530
- I mean, yeah, there's like two tests

01:31:48.530 --> 01:31:50.300
when you get here and your test before.

01:31:50.300 --> 01:31:52.540
Obviously, somehow, someone
did get COVID on my flight

01:31:52.540 --> 01:31:54.120
but that was caught

01:31:54.120 --> 01:31:55.987
and then if you test
positive in the three days

01:31:55.987 --> 01:31:57.250
you have to...

01:31:57.250 --> 01:31:59.040
I understand it can still slip through

01:31:59.040 --> 01:32:01.650
but also it feels like
such diminishing returns

01:32:01.650 --> 01:32:04.340
at this point, to keep this rule in place.

01:32:04.340 --> 01:32:05.210
You know, I mean it's whatever,

01:32:05.210 --> 01:32:06.880
I'm sure everyone will have
a personal opinion about it

01:32:06.880 --> 01:32:07.713
and that stuff.

01:32:07.713 --> 01:32:09.180
I understand allowing tourists in,

01:32:09.180 --> 01:32:11.460
obviously I get that
this is like, whatever.

01:32:11.460 --> 01:32:14.476
- There like different
levels, there's tourists

01:32:14.476 --> 01:32:16.180
which is opening the floodgates

01:32:16.180 --> 01:32:18.150
but then there's people
who are literally waiting

01:32:18.150 --> 01:32:20.910
on a working visa.
- It breaks my heart, man.

01:32:20.910 --> 01:32:22.197
I really feel sorry for these people

01:32:22.197 --> 01:32:23.930
who had their life lined up to come here

01:32:23.930 --> 01:32:26.130
and they've just been just
hanging around, waiting.

01:32:26.130 --> 01:32:27.930
Really, I do feel so sorry for them.

01:32:28.930 --> 01:32:30.930
It's so fucked, it's really fucked.

01:32:30.930 --> 01:32:31.920
- Well, hopefully soon.

01:32:31.920 --> 01:32:34.343
I mean the the cases are
going down a lot now.

01:32:35.555 --> 01:32:37.690
- I saw an article today that was like,

01:32:37.690 --> 01:32:40.947
'Japan's drop in COVID
cases baffles experts.'

01:32:40.947 --> 01:32:43.070
(all laughing)

01:32:43.070 --> 01:32:44.760
But also I heard that
Japan isn't testing as much

01:32:44.760 --> 01:32:46.828
so I mean yeah yeah...

01:32:46.828 --> 01:32:47.830
- But I mean it's also because like

01:32:47.830 --> 01:32:51.363
most young people now are
finally fucking vaccinating.

01:32:51.363 --> 01:32:54.060
- Have we missed anything
since we've been gone?

01:32:54.060 --> 01:32:56.220
- I mean the country's
opened back up again.

01:32:56.220 --> 01:32:58.527
I mean in terms of like
the the 'lock down.'

01:33:00.450 --> 01:33:03.777
So beginning of October they were like,

01:33:03.777 --> 01:33:06.163
"Oh, yeah so everything's just good now.

01:33:07.050 --> 01:33:09.790
Everything's open, you can
drink alcohol if you want."

01:33:09.790 --> 01:33:12.990
Everyone's like, "Are you sure?"

01:33:12.990 --> 01:33:14.666
'Cause you said that last time...

01:33:14.666 --> 01:33:15.780
(group chattering)

01:33:15.780 --> 01:33:18.220
We did that last time we
could only do it for a week

01:33:18.220 --> 01:33:20.001
before you shut that shit down again.

01:33:20.001 --> 01:33:20.834
(Garnt laughing)

01:33:20.834 --> 01:33:22.740
- It was just like, the
floodgates were open,

01:33:22.740 --> 01:33:24.210
everyone went out drinking

01:33:24.210 --> 01:33:25.897
and then a week later
everyone's just like,

01:33:25.897 --> 01:33:29.134
"Well, that was a good time."

01:33:29.134 --> 01:33:30.017
- Experts were like,

01:33:30.017 --> 01:33:31.610
"Yeah, that's a bad
idea, let's not do that."

01:33:31.610 --> 01:33:33.273
- The Japanese government
managed to do something

01:33:33.273 --> 01:33:35.460
that I think they've never done before,

01:33:35.460 --> 01:33:37.340
test the patience of their population

01:33:37.340 --> 01:33:38.320
and piss them off.

01:33:38.320 --> 01:33:40.410
I've never seen people
get so actually angry

01:33:40.410 --> 01:33:41.512
about shit in Japan.

01:33:41.512 --> 01:33:42.460
It just doesn't happen,

01:33:42.460 --> 01:33:44.390
but people actually
got so angry about them

01:33:44.390 --> 01:33:45.510
keeping extending the lockdown

01:33:45.510 --> 01:33:48.180
- Yeah, because they're so
fucking wishy-washy as well.

01:33:48.180 --> 01:33:50.390
They're like, "Oh, yeah, so
the cases are going down,

01:33:50.390 --> 01:33:52.520
it's not zero, but it's going down

01:33:52.520 --> 01:33:54.853
so maybe we can open it up again."

01:33:54.853 --> 01:33:58.063
And then it goes back up and they're like,

01:33:58.063 --> 01:34:01.503
Experts are baffled.
- Surprised Pikachu face.

01:34:01.503 --> 01:34:02.990
- Experts are baffled.

01:34:02.990 --> 01:34:03.823
How did this happen?

01:34:03.823 --> 01:34:04.700
It was going down.

01:34:04.700 --> 01:34:06.650
- And the Olympics just like blew it up.

01:34:06.650 --> 01:34:08.930
- Oh, my God, yeah.

01:34:08.930 --> 01:34:11.020
- Oh, my God, just like I watched a video

01:34:11.020 --> 01:34:14.470
about all the fuck ups of the
Olympics and it was insane.

01:34:14.470 --> 01:34:16.720
Having it all in one video,

01:34:16.720 --> 01:34:18.530
the sheer amount of people that got fired

01:34:18.530 --> 01:34:20.220
off the Olympic committee is insane.

01:34:20.220 --> 01:34:21.053
- It was like half of them.

01:34:21.053 --> 01:34:24.240
- Yeah, and then the amount
of controversy, it was insane.

01:34:24.240 --> 01:34:25.520
I was like this is fucking terrible.

01:34:25.520 --> 01:34:27.040
- It was so fucking weird.
- Oh, my God.

01:34:27.040 --> 01:34:29.700
- I mean so far it seems
to be going all right.

01:34:29.700 --> 01:34:33.070
I mean the other day I was at a park

01:34:33.070 --> 01:34:34.260
and with some of my friends

01:34:34.260 --> 01:34:36.110
and someone was like,

01:34:36.110 --> 01:34:37.610
we should do a bold gamer move.

01:34:37.610 --> 01:34:39.970
We should drink a beer in
this park, and I was like...

01:34:39.970 --> 01:34:42.490
It felt like someone
just offered me cocaine.

01:34:42.490 --> 01:34:43.410
I was like no no,

01:34:43.410 --> 01:34:44.840
I don't think that's a good idea.

01:34:44.840 --> 01:34:48.040
I think someone's watching,
this this doesn't feel right.

01:34:48.040 --> 01:34:50.240
I did it, it was very liberating but...

01:34:50.240 --> 01:34:51.440
- Fuck the police.
- Yeah, I was like

01:34:51.440 --> 01:34:53.440
fuck the police, they can't stop us now.

01:34:54.410 --> 01:34:56.190
Yeah, I mean, I don't know.

01:34:56.190 --> 01:34:58.170
I'm just waiting again for next week

01:34:58.170 --> 01:34:59.507
for the government to be like,

01:34:59.507 --> 01:35:00.603
"Changed our minds.

01:35:01.510 --> 01:35:02.343
It's lock down again."

01:35:02.343 --> 01:35:04.360
- Well, the real question
is, is karaoke open?

01:35:04.360 --> 01:35:06.145
'cause that's
- Is that true?

01:35:06.145 --> 01:35:06.978
- Everything is open.
- That's how you know

01:35:06.978 --> 01:35:08.050
lock down's actually ended.

01:35:08.050 --> 01:35:09.060
Once the karaoke opens,

01:35:09.060 --> 01:35:10.690
that's like the equivalent of when

01:35:10.690 --> 01:35:12.190
the British pubs were open.

01:35:12.190 --> 01:35:13.960
- So the karaokes are open,

01:35:13.960 --> 01:35:16.190
restaurants now go past eight o'clock

01:35:16.190 --> 01:35:17.160
you can order alcohol,

